id: 00001006020000
title: Supported Metadata Keys
role: manual
tags: #manual #meta #reference #zettel #zettelstore
syntax: zmk
created: 20210126175322
modified: 20261121201152

Although you are free to define your own metadata, by using any key (according to the [[syntax|00001006010000]]), some keys have a special meaning that is enforced by Zettelstore.
See the computed [[list of supported metadata keys|00000000000090]] for details.

Most keys conform to a [[type|00001006030000]].

Every metadata key belongs to exactly one of three categories:

; ""user""
: The value is set by the user.
  This is the category of most keys, including all user-defined keys.
; ""managed""
: The value is set and maintained by Zettelstore and is stored in the zettel.
  Zettelstore maintains the value only for zettel that are created or changed through Zettelstore.
  If a zettel is created or changed outside of Zettelstore, e.g. with an editor, the value of [[''created''|#created]] and [[''modified''|#modified]] should be set manually.
  Managed metadata is not shown as ordinary metadata in the web user interface.
  How a stored value is used depends on the key:
  [[''created''|#created]] is taken from the zettel if it is stored there, and is calculated otherwise.
  [[''modified''|#modified]] is set to the current time whenever the zettel is stored.
  [[''id''|#id]] is derived from the box that contains the zettel, e.g. from the name of the file.
; ""property""
: The value is always calculated by Zettelstore and is never stored.
  A value that is stored in a zettel is ignored.
  An example is [[''folge''|#folge]], which is calculated from the metadata [[''precursor''|#precursor]] of all zettel that reference this zettel.

The following user keys are __invertible__: for each of them, Zettelstore calculates the inverse references as a property.

|=User key       |=Calculated property
|''precursor''   |''folge''
|''predecessor'' |''successor''
|''prequel''     |''sequel''
|''superordinate'' |''subordinate''

The following list describes the supported metadata keys in alphabetical order.

; [!author|''author'']
: A string value describing the author of a zettel.
  If given, it will be shown in the [[web user interface|00001014000000]] for the zettel.
; [!back|''back'']
: Is a property that contains the identifiers of all zettel that reference the zettel of this metadata, that are not referenced by this zettel.
  Basically, it is the value of [[''backward''|#backward]], but without any zettel identifier that is contained in [[''forward''|#forward]].
; [!backward|''backward'']
: Is a property that contains the identifiers of all zettel that reference the zettel of this metadata.
  References within invertible values are not included here, e.g. [[''precursor''|#precursor]].
; [!box-name|''box-name'']
: A word that names the [[box|00001004011200]] from which the zettel was retrieved.

  This is a property.
; [!copyright|''copyright'']
: Defines a copyright string that will be encoded.
  If not given, the value ''default-copyright'' from the [[configuration zettel|00001004020000#default-copyright]] will be used.
; [!created|''created'']
: Date and time when a zettel was created through Zettelstore.
  If you create a zettel with an editor software outside Zettelstore, you should set it manually to an appropriate value.

  This is a managed value.
  If you work through Zettelstore, the value is set automatically.

  If it is not stored within a zettel, it will be computed based on the value of the [[Zettel Identifier|00001006050000]]: if it contains a value >= 19700101000000, it will be coerced to a date/time; otherwise the version time of the running software will be used.

  Please note that the value of ''created'' will be different (in most cases) to the value of [[''id''|#id]] / the zettel identifier, because it is exact up to the second.
  When calculating a zettel identifier, Zettelstore tries to set the second value to zero, if possible.
; [!credential|''credential'']
: Contains the hashed password, as it was emitted by [[``zettelstore password``|00001004051400]].
  It is internally created by hashing the password, the [[zettel identifier|00001006050000]], and the value of the [[''user-id''|#user-id]] key.

  It is only used for zettel with a ''role'' value of ""user"".
; [!dead|''dead'']
: Property that contains all references of the zettel that point to a zettel identifier for which no zettel exists.
  References to external resources, e.g. URLs, are not included.
; [!expire|''expire'']
: A user-entered timestamp that records the point in time when the zettel should expire.
  When a zettel expires, Zettelstore does nothing.
  It is up to you to define required actions.
  ''expire'' is just a documentation.
  You could define a query and execute it regularly, for example [[query:expire? ORDER expire]].
  Alternatively, a Zettelstore client software could define some actions when it detects expired zettel.
; [!folge|''folge'']
: Is a property that contains identifiers of all zettel that reference this zettel via the [[''precursor''|#precursor]] value.

  It is used to reference __Folgezettel__, those that develop the idea of the current zettel a bit further, following a ""train of thought.""
; [!folge-role|''folge-role'']
: Serves as a reminder of the [[''role''|#role]] that this zettel should get later, if its current role is only preliminary.
; [!forward|''forward'']
: Property that contains all references that identify another zettel within the content of the zettel.
; [!id|''id'']
: Contains the [[zettel identifier|00001006050000]], as given by the Zettelstore.
  It is a managed value.
  The box that contains the zettel determines the identifier.
  A value entered by hand in the metadata does not change the identifier of a zettel whose file name contains an identifier.

  Whenever Zettelstore stores the zettel, it also writes the identifier into the metadata of the zettel.
  This stored value is only a fallback, for the case that the file is renamed in such a way that its name no longer contains an identifier.
  If the name of the file contains an identifier, that one is used and the stored value is ignored.
; [!index-state|''index-state'']
: Is a property that is set only if the search index cannot provide all property values for the zettel.
  If it is set, the properties that depend on the search index are not calculated.
  If the key is not present, the property values are complete.
  A value that is stored in the zettel is ignored.

  The following values are possible:

  ''incomplete'': The initial indexing of all zettel after the start of Zettelstore is not yet complete.
  A later rebuild of the index does not lead to this value, because the previous index continues to serve requests.
  See [[Retrieve administrative data|00001012070500]] for how to find out whether the initial indexing is complete.

  ''unindexed'': The initial indexing is complete, but the search index does not know this zettel, e.g. because the zettel was created or changed just now.
; [!lang|''lang'']
: Language for the zettel.
  Mostly used for HTML rendering of the zettel.

  If not given, the value ''lang'' from the zettel of the [[current user|00001010040200]] will be used.
  If that value is also not available, the value from the [[configuration zettel|00001004020000#lang]] will be used.
  Use values according to the language definition of [[RFC-5646|https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5646]].
; [!license|''license'']
: Defines a license string that will be rendered.
  If not given, the value ''default-license'' from the [[configuration zettel|00001004020000#default-license]] will be used.
; [!modified|''modified'']
: Date and time when a zettel was modified through Zettelstore.
  If you edit a zettel with an editor software outside Zettelstore, you should set it manually to an appropriate value.

  This is a managed value.
  If you work through Zettelstore, the value is set automatically.
; [!precursor|''precursor'']
: References the zettel that this zettel continues directly, i.e. this zettel is a __Folgezettel__ of the referenced zettel: it develops the idea of the referenced zettel further, following a ""train of thought.""
  The inverse relation is calculated as property [[''folge''|#folge]].
  Use [[''predecessor''|#predecessor]] for a looser follow-up relation.
; [!predecessor|''predecessor'']
: References zettel of which this zettel is a later version, a result, or a continuation.
  Use it if the relation does not form a train of thought, or if the referenced zettel cannot or should not be changed to link to this zettel.
  The inverse relation is calculated as property [[''successor''|#successor]].
  Use [[''precursor''|#precursor]] for a direct continuation of an idea.
; [!prequel|''prequel'']
: Specifies one or more zettel that are conceptually a prequel zettel.
  These are zettel that occurred somehow before the current zettel.
  Basically the inverse of key [[''sequel''|#sequel]].
; [!published|''published'']
: This property contains the timestamp of the last modification or creation of the zettel.
  If [[''modified''|#modified]] is set to a valid timestamp, it holds that value.
  Otherwise, if [[''created''|#created]] is set to a valid timestamp, ''published'' contains its value.
  If neither ''modified'' nor ''created'' are set, and the zettel identifier contains a valid timestamp, the identifier is used.
  In all other cases, this property is not set.

  It can be used for [[sorting|00001007700000]] zettel based on their publication date.

  It is a property.
  There is no need to set it via Zettelstore.
; [!query|''query'']
: Stores the [[query|00001007031140]] that was used to create the zettel.
  This is for future reference.
; [!read-only|''read-only'']
: Marks a zettel as read-only.
  The interpretation of [[supported values|00001006020400]] for this key depends on whether authentication is [[enabled|00001010040100]] or not.
; [!role|''role'']
: Defines the role of the zettel.
  Can be used for selecting zettel.
  See [[supported zettel roles|00001006020100]].
  If not given, it is ignored.
; [!see-also|''see-also'']
: References other zettel that might be relevant.
  The WebUI renders these zettel as an unordered list under the heading ""See also"".

; [!see-also|''see-also'']
: A set of [[zettel identifiers|00001006050000]] of zettel that belong to an extended context of this zettel, possibly of a different topic.
  It is a systematic alternative to a list of references in the content of the zettel.
  Duplicate and invalid identifiers are ignored.

  The references are handled as if they were given in the content of the zettel.
  They are part of [[''forward''|#forward]], and the referenced zettel contain this zettel in [[''backward''|#backward]] and [[''back''|#back]].
  Identifiers of non-existing zettel are not shown, but are part of [[''dead''|#dead]].
  There is no inverse property, the relation is intentionally one-sided.

  The web user interface shows the titles of the referenced zettel as a list under the heading ""See also"", ordered by zettel identifier.

  In contrast to [[''precursor''|#precursor]], [[''predecessor''|#predecessor]], [[''prequel''|#prequel]] and [[''superordinate''|#superordinate]], ''see-also'' does not express a specific relation between the zettel.
; [!sequel|''sequel'']
: Is a property that contains identifiers of all zettel that reference this zettel through the [[''prequel''|#prequel]] value.

  A __sequel zettel__ acts as a branching thought of the current zettel.
; [!subordinate|''subordinate'']
: Is a property that contains identifiers of all zettel that reference this zettel through the [[''superordinate''|#superordinate]] value.
; [!successor|''successor'']
: Is a property that contains identifiers of all zettel that reference this zettel via the [[''predecessor''|#predecessor]] value.

  It is used to reference zettel that are somehow a follow-up zettel, but cannot / should not be referenced in the zettel content.
; [!summary|''summary'']
: Summarizes the content of the zettel using plain text.
; [!superordinate|''superordinate'']
: Specifies a zettel that is conceptually a superordinate zettel.
  This might be a more abstract zettel, or a zettel that should be higher in a hierarchy.
; [!syntax|''syntax'']
: Specifies the syntax that should be used for interpreting the zettel.
  The zettel about [[other markup languages|00001008000000]] defines supported values.
  If it is not given, it defaults to ""plain"".
; [!tags|''tags'']
: Contains a space separated list of tags to describe the zettel further.
  Each Tag must begin with the number sign character (""''#''"", U+0023).
; [!title|''title'']
: Specifies the title of the zettel.
  If not given, the value of [[''id''|#id]] will be used.
; [!url|''url'']
: Defines a URL / URI for this zettel that possibly references external material.
  One use case is to specify the document that the current zettel comments on.
  The URL will be rendered special in the [[web user interface|00001014000000]] if you use the default template.
; [!useless-files|''useless-files'']
: Contains the file names that are rejected to serve the content of a zettel.
  Is used for [[directory boxes|00001004011400]] and [[file boxes|00001004011200#file]].
  If a zettel is deleted, these files will also be deleted.

  This is a property.
; [!user-id|''user-id'']
: Provides some unique user identification for an [[user zettel|00001010040200]].
  It is used as a user name for authentication.

  It is only used for zettel with a ''role'' value of ""user"".
; [!user-role|''user-role'']
: Defines the basic privileges of an authenticated user, e.g. reading / changing zettel.
  Is only valid in a user zettel.

  See [[User roles|00001010070300]] for more details.
; [!visibility|''visibility'']
: When you work with authentication, you can give every zettel a value to decide, who can see the zettel.
  Its default value can be set with [[''default-visibility''|00001004020000#default-visibility]] of the configuration zettel.

  See [[visibility rules for zettel|00001010070200]] for more details.